<item>
            <title>[IGNITE-11195] Platform C++ tests failed to find JVM for Java 11 build</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-11195</link>
                <project id="12315922" key="IGNITE">Ignite</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;482 C++ tests failed with error&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;preformatted panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;preformattedContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;std::exception: JVM library is not found (did you set JAVA_HOME environment variable?)
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://ci.ignite.apache.org/viewLog.html?buildId=2973675&amp;amp;buildTypeId=IgniteTests24Java8_PlatformCWinX64Release&amp;amp;tab=buildResultsDiv&amp;amp;branch_IgniteTests24Java8=ignite-11155&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://ci.ignite.apache.org/viewLog.html?buildId=2973675&amp;amp;buildTypeId=IgniteTests24Java8_PlatformCWinX64Release&amp;amp;tab=buildResultsDiv&amp;amp;branch_IgniteTests24Java8=ignite-11155&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Looks like we need somehow handle new parameters in C++ tests&lt;/p&gt;</description>
